 "result_text": "I fixed both problems in `pythonfmu/fmi2slave.py`. I haven't run anything, so neither fix is tested. I also didn't generate an FMU or validate it with `fmpy`.\n\n- **Float error:** the start time, stop time and tolerance are now converted with `str()` before they go into the XML. You can pass plain floats, e.g. `DefaultExperiment(start_time=0.0, stop_time=1.0)`, and the `str(0.)` workaround is no longer needed.\n- **`fmpy` validation error:** this was on the PythonFMU side, not `fmpy`. The FMI 2.0 schema requires `DefaultExperiment` to come before `ModelVariables`. PythonFMU was writing it at the end, after `ModelStructure`. It's now written right after `LogCategories` and before `ModelVariables`.",
